/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
|  stripper01/0/feed -- sour water on the apparent component basis.             |
|                                                                              |
|  The same three roles as column13 (water the solvent, NH3 the cation route,   |
|  CO2 the anion route + the molecular CO2aq), fed UNEQUAL on purpose so the    |
|  charge balance is a real test and not a symmetry.  The load is heavier than  |
|  column13's (2.5 mol% NH3, 1 mol% CO2): a stripper feed, not a trace.         |
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
componentMolarFlows
{
    NH3       2.5   kmol/h;
    CO2       1.0   kmol/h;
    H2S       0.5   kmol/h;
    water    96.0   kmol/h;
}

T               360.0 K;
P               101325 Pa;

//  THE FEED'S THERMAL STATE, DECLARED (2026-09-12).  It used to be stated only
//  as `feedQuality 1.0;` in the column's operation block -- a second home for a
//  fact the stream owns, which the first-law report never saw: the report
//  resolved this unpinned (T, P, z) to its own equilibrium, found it two-phase,
//  and priced it there while the column priced a liquid.  That disagreement WAS
//  this plant's entire energy residual.  The declaration now lives here, once.
//
//  READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING IT.  A declared vapour fraction is a PIN: the
//  engine honours it and does not re-solve the state (R-E2).  This feed's own
//  equilibrium at 360 K and 1 atm is NOT single-phase -- see the case README --
//  so what is declared here is the author's saturated-liquid charge, not the
//  flash of it.  If you want the column fed by the equilibrium instead, delete
//  this line and the engine will resolve it; the answer will move.
vaporFraction   0.0;
